II - Ability to apply knowledge and understanding The training program of the Master's Degree Course in Medical and Pharmaceutical Biotechnologies is structured in activities that allow the graduate to acquire:
- ability to apply knowledge of key aspects of cellular and molecular biology involved in pathological processes, of human interest and of different origin, to innovative approaches especially in the scientific/technological development in the biomedical field and in the design of biotechnological strategies in the clinical/experimental and pharmaceutical field;
- skills and competencies in recognizing elements of innovation, limitations and potential in the development projects of biotechnologies and in the design and application of new diagnostic strategies;
- ability to critically analyze the information provided by laboratory medicine;
- critical ability to process data in the application of molecular biology, biochemistry and bioinformatics methodologies;
- ability to monitor advanced technologies applied in the clinical/experimental field and apply molecular technologies and recombinant DNA and advanced biotechnologies for personalized therapeutic and diagnostic approaches;
- ability to evaluate compliance with the main aspects of bioethics in the development of experimental protocols;
- ability to organize and plan research or development activities of biotechnological products, demonstrating methodological application skills;
- ability to evaluate with competence the use of biopharmaceuticals, the various phases of clinical testing and validation and to discuss the key aspects leading to specific choices;
- ability to integrate biological, physiological, pathological, statistical, analytical, legislative data in the design/application of biotechnological/biomedical/pharmaceutical models/methodologies;
- ability to develop study methods and appropriate methodological paths, to select and interpret data and information and to work towards specific objectives;
- ability to make autonomous judgments and to learn autonomously, which supports the ability to operate with a critical and motivated approach to the choices made
- ability to present/transmit/disseminate one's knowledge, actions and information;
- critical and creative ability to plan strategies to be undertaken, to identify the appropriate resources/approaches to be applied, to monitor the impact of actions taken in order to achieve specific objectives or solve problems/questions.

