The knowledge and skills acquired allow the biotechnologist specialized in the medical and pharmaceutical field to carry out the following functions:
- organize, design with operational autonomy and coordinate interdisciplinary protocols of basic and applied research, aimed at expanding and innovating scientific knowledge and its application in the scientific and technical-productive field of sectors such as the chemical-pharmaceutical, therapeutic and medical-diagnostic sector;
- organize and carry out laboratory activities, basic and advanced diagnostic investigations requiring the use of innovative biotechnological methodologies (molecular, genetic, cellular, omics and bioinformatic);
- assist, within the areas of competence provided for by current regulations, professional figures in the medical area in the development and experimental testing of innovative diagnostic/therapeutic products also involving the manipulation of genetic/biological material/engineered cells;
- develop, design, formulate and experiment, on the basis of chemical, biological and toxicological aspects, new biotechnological products and biopharmaceuticals collaborating, also in the management of innovation projects and in activities of marketing, in teams with other professional figures with specific backgrounds for the discipline;
- participate and carry out functions and activities of evaluation, monitoring and validation of clinical studies in various therapeutic areas according to current regulations;
- participate in the development and/or evaluation to proceed with the application of patents in the biomedical field;
- conduct and coordinate programs for the development, monitoring and prevention and diagnosis through the management of advanced biotechnological/biomedical technologies;
- deal with scientific dissemination and/or consulting activities with public and private bodies/biotech companies.

