The Applied Data Scientist is able to:
- identify, classify and process the data in the possession of an organization in a specific application domain, with attention to the quality of the data and the rules that govern its processing;
- identify which data should be acquired outside the organization and the related acquisition methods, also in economic and legal terms;
- apply the techniques of Computer Science, Statistics and Mathematics relevant to the processing of large amounts of data and to formulate innovative, qualitative and quantitative answers to complex problems that require a multi- and interdisciplinary approach;
- explore, validate, model and analyze data to add value to the organization, both in terms of process and in terms of product;
- identify and use the most effective software, hardware and network infrastructures for the processing of (big) data, and manage the problems related to their reliability and security;
- communicate effectively the data and the results of the analyses carried out, both in written and oral form, also through advanced techniques of visualization and representation of information;
- understand the problems and evaluate the ethical and legal impacts connected to the processing and use of data;
- demonstrate the effectiveness of the proposed solutions;
- dialogue, also in English, and operate effectively with experts from the various application sectors in order to understand the needs of the sector and to suggest effective technical solutions;
- continuously update and connect with the most advanced international realities in the field.

